hinge.act strict semantic rebind audit (2026-08-17)

User decision
  Require strict agreement between the certified Lean declaration and the Julia checker;
  do not retain an exact classification by interpreting a Set-valued declaration as an
  unstated nonemptiness proposition.

Mismatch
  ERIEC.Hinge.Act returns Set M.
  check_hinge returns Bool and decides whether that set is nonempty.
  The former catalog binding therefore did not have the codomain or proposition stated by
  the checker guarantee.

Correction
  Add the definitional predicate ERIEC.Hinge.ActNonempty := (Act ...).Nonempty.
  Rebind VP-HNG-001 / hinge.act to ActNonempty and bind both juliaSymbol and juliaChecker to
  check_hinge. Preserve ERIEC.Hinge.Act and every existing Julia method unchanged.

Classification
  exact_finite_decision remains justified: rho_rel, sigma_rel, kappa, and epsilon are the
  supplied relation data; check_hinge independently computes their finite Act intersection
  and returns exactly its nonemptiness. It consumes no proof Bool or obligation callback.

Invariants
  The M3 nonempty-hinge judgment is preserved. No axiom or object is added, no tolerance,
  fixture, seed, phenomenal_claim, sensitivity case, or contract ID changes, and no commit
  or push is performed.
